From c03421d31aeb7c12a56f63c083e1183fb3f27092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:57:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] grate: clear the PSEQ command slots through the even slots
 only

grate_init_state() cleared the 16 sequencer command pairs with one
32-word write to PSEQ_COMMAND_EVEN(0), which also writes the 16 odd
slots at 0x521 + 2n. The odd slots hold the buffer address of a DMA
command, and kernel patch 0031 makes the Grate command stream patcher
read every word written to them as a relocation descriptor. The zeros
of the clear would then be patched with the address of buffer 0, and a
job without buffers would fail.

Write the 16 even slots with one single-word packet each. Nothing
reads a command slot that is not part of the program that is about to
run, so leaving the odd slots alone does not change a draw. The
packet is one word longer per pair, 32 words instead of 33.

Checked: the file compiles for armv7 with the compile command of the
0045 image build. Not run on the tablet yet; needs kernel patch 0031
(new version, drivers/gpu/drm/grate) to see any effect, and must ship
together with it.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
index ef1b222a552..e9f34378a51 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/grate/grate_draw.c
@@ -247,9 +247,16 @@ grate_init_state(struct grate_context *context, uint32_t **ptrp)
    GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_PSEQ_TIMEOUT, 0));
    GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_PSEQ_PC, 0));
 
-   GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_incr(REG_TGR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_EVEN(0), 32));
-   for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++)
+   /*
+    * Clear the sequencer commands. Only the even slots are written: the
+    * kernel treats every word written to an odd slot as the relocation of
+    * a DMA address.
+    */
+   for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++) {
+      GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_incr(
+                                REG_TGR3D_PSEQ_COMMAND_EVEN(i), 1));
       GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, 0);
+   }
 
    GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_PSEQ_INST_OFFSET, 0));
    GRATE_PUSHBUF_WORD(ptr, host1x_opcode_imm(REG_TGR3D_PSEQ_DBG_X, 0));
-- 
